  "evidence": "TEXT_D: NHS +£540m/year, recruit 10,000 nurses or 5,000 doctors, maximum 6‑month waits, free eye/dental checks, stronger community care and a new Carer’s Benefit; end rough sleeping by 2000; national insulation for 2m lowest‑income households; strong equal‑rights agenda (women, disabled, minorities, LGBT), equal age of consent, repeal Section 28, tackle hate crime; Bill of Rights, Human Rights Commission, PR for all elections; raise personal allowance, introduce a 50% rate over £100k, minimum income guarantee for older people, simpler Low Income Benefit; 3,000 more police, faster justice; maintain defence capability, keep Trident, support NATO. TEXT_E: Rebuild the NHS, treat 100,000 extra patients, end cancer waits, annual real‑terms spending increases, ban tobacco ads, create a Food Standards Agency; welfare‑to‑work for 250,000 under‑25s, national childcare strategy, carers’ rights, restore duty to house priority homeless, reinvest council house receipts; National Minimum Wage via Low Pay Commission, union recognition, uprate Child Benefit; no rise in income tax rates, golden rule and Bank of England reform; tough on crime and its causes, halve time to sentencing, Youth Offender Teams, sentencing guidelines, free vote to ban handguns; defence rooted in NATO, retain Trident; incorporate ECHR, FOI, end hereditary peers’ voting rights, devolution.",
